From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:10:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] tccgen: inline the calls of always_inline functions and of
 static functions given a tested constant

The call of an __always_inline function, or of a merely static function
given a constant argument that its body tests, is compiled in place of a
call (inline_call()): the arguments, evaluated and converted as for the
call, initialise locals named as the parameters in a scope of their own,
so that a constant argument is a known local and folds in the body as any
known local does (the constant propagation through locals); the body is
parsed from the token string that is kept for every static or inline
function (an __always_inline function that is neither is kept now too),
with a label stack of its own, the kprop label scan and the pragma
replay; a return stores to a result variable, itself a kprop local, and
jumps to the end of the body; the caller's locals and labels are unlinked
from the identifier table around the body and relinked after it (only
those that are linked: a statement expression's locals stay on
local_stack unlinked); funcname, the return type and the switch, loop and
kprop state of the caller are saved around it; the body's stack space is
given back (the frame takes the low-water mark).  Not inlined: in dead
code, under -g or -b, variadic or old-style functions, bodies with a
static local, recursion, a nesting deeper than 24, and a merely static
function from within another one's inlined body, or longer than 1024
tokens, or whose constant parameter appears in no condition (the
parentheses of if, while, switch, for, or next to !, ?, &&, ||, ==, !=):
inlining every static function given a constant grew mm/page_alloc.o's
text 2.6 times.

The Linux kernel relies on inlining in an optimizing compiler where an
"i" asm operand is taken from a parameter of an __always_inline function
(rip_rel_ptr()'s "leaq %c1(%%rip), %0" : "=r"(p) : "i"(p), the asm goto
of __static_cpu_has() with "i"(bit), "i"(1 << (bit & 7)) and the address
of a capability byte) and where a canary is called under a condition on a
parameter (__bad_mask() behind field_multiplier()'s mask check in every
FIELD_PREP() user, vma_thp_gfp_mask() behind "if (order)" in
__swap_cache_alloc(), __scoped_seqlock_invalid_target() behind the switch
on the target of __scoped_seqlock_next()); the tinycc-os-kernel project
worked around them with four kernel patches, which this removes (fix 120).

What the kernel's bodies needed with it: a known local may hold the
address of a symbol of file scope (Sym.ksym; not a string literal's or a
static local's, whose Sym dies with its block), so that rip_rel_ptr(&x)
has its "i" operand and a test of a known function pointer folds (the
address of a symbol that is not weak compared with 0, gen_opic and
kcond); an asm's outputs are invalidated after its inputs were read
("=r"(p) : "i"(p)); asm goto targets are gotos for the label scan; a loop
that assigns a variable only the constant it holds at the head, a literal
or a call of a function that folds to it (order = next_order(&orders,
order) without THP), keeps it known (struct kkill cond; the function must
be a call at every mention in the loop); the constraints "I", "N", "M"
take only 0-31, 0-255, 0-3 and "e" a 32-bit signed value ("Ir"(65) of a
bt, "er"(1 << 40) of arch_atomic64_or() are registers), and an
instruction without a suffix, an immediate and a memory operand ("bt $0,
(%rax)", an "Ir" operand that became a constant) takes the mode's word
with GNU as's warning instead of "cannot infer opcode suffix" (test 155's
test_bit() gets the kernel's explicit size); __builtin_constant_p() of a
non-constant makes the stub-fold probe impure (return
__builtin_constant_p(x); folded to 0 for every call); a cleanup call's
save_lvalues() stops at the inlined call's vstack base (it turned the
enclosing assignment's destination into a temporary).
